# Build-time configuration for MarCom.
#
# Vite inlines VITE_* variables at BUILD time, so every value here is a property
# of the artifact you produce, not a runtime toggle. Changing one means a
# rebuild. Copy to `.env.local` for local overrides (git-ignored).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_IS_MENU_VISIBLE — does this build draw its own navigation chrome?
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# true   the module is the whole application: sidebar, topbar and help rail are
#        rendered. This is what local development and the hosted demo need.
# false  a host platform frames this module: only the routed page content
#        renders, so the user does not get two menus and two identity chips
#        stacked on one screen.
#
# Unset it and the build decides: chrome ON while developing, OFF in a
# production build. An unrecognised value (a typo) falls back to that default
# rather than reading as false — a mistyped flag should not blank the menu.
#
# IMPORTANT for the hosted demo: `vercel build` is a production build, so it
# takes the default and ships WITHOUT the menu. The demo must set this
# explicitly:
#     VITE_IS_MENU_VISIBLE=true npx vercel build --prod
#
# VITE_IS_MENU_VISIBLE=true

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_DEMO_PACK — which industry dataset the build loads
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# One of: default | renewable | cloud | lifesciences
# Unset uses `default` (the Aureon consumer/enterprise technology dataset).
# An unknown value warns in the console and falls back to `default`.
# See docs/DEMO_PACKS.md.
#
# VITE_DEMO_PACK=renewable
